research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl-36-{"id":"def-limits-at-infinity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limit_of_a_function"],"rationale":"The source gives the standard finite limits at plus/minus infinity and infinite limits using real thresholds. The local definition adds nonvacuity hypotheses and refuses extended-real equation notation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl:37:{"id":"thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_limoffunc.html"],"rationale":"Lebl states the same Heine criterion for every sequence in the punctured domain converging to c. The local proof adapts the standard contrapositive construction and exposes its countable-choice step.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl-38-{"id":"cor-sequential-criterion-for-nonexistence","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_limoffunc.html"],"rationale":"Lebl’s exact sequential criterion immediately yields both local nonexistence tests. The local corollary packages the two-sequence and nonconvergent-image variants and records that only the choice-free direction is used.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl-39-{"id":"lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_limoffunc.html"],"rationale":"Lebl states that a function with a finite limit is bounded on a punctured neighborhood, with the standard |L|+1 bound. The local proof writes the estimate directly.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl-40-{"id":"lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_limoffunc.html"],"rationale":"The standard limit inequalities in Lebl give eventual sign preservation and a positive lower bound away from zero for a nonzero limit. The local statement packages both signs and the limit-point consequence for the nonzero domain.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
