research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1451-**Everything below is proved directly from $\varepsilon$ and $\delta$.** No
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1452-sequence is constructed and no choice principle is used, so all four claims are
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1453-theorems of ZF. Passing through
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md:1454:[[thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits]] instead would import the
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1455-countable choice spent in that theorem's converse direction, for no gain; see
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1456-[[rem-heine-criterion-choice-cost]].
