research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/thm-algebra-of-function-limits.md-74-sequence is constructed and no choice principle is used, so all four claims are
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/thm-algebra-of-function-limits.md-75-theorems of ZF. Passing through
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/thm-algebra-of-function-limits.md:76:[[thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits]] instead would import the
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/thm-algebra-of-function-limits.md-77-countable choice spent in that theorem's converse direction, for no gain; see
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/thm-algebra-of-function-limits.md-78-[[rem-heine-criterion-choice-cost]].
