research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cex-dirichlet-has-no-limit-anywhere.md-768-**Only the choice-free half of the Heine criterion is used.** The proof runs the
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cex-dirichlet-has-no-limit-anywhere.md-769-implication from condition 1 to condition 2 of
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cex-dirichlet-has-no-limit-anywhere.md:770:[[thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits]], which is a theorem of ZF; no
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cex-dirichlet-has-no-limit-anywhere.md-771-sequence is constructed here, both being supplied by the hypothesis. So this
