research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-sequential-criterion-for-nonexistence.prompt.md-136-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-sequential-criterion-for-nonexistence.prompt.md-137-**Only the choice-free half of the Heine criterion is used.** The proof runs the
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-sequential-criterion-for-nonexistence.prompt.md-138-implication from condition 1 to condition 2 of
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-sequential-criterion-for-nonexistence.prompt.md:139:[[thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits]], which is a theorem of ZF; no
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-sequential-criterion-for-nonexistence.prompt.md-140-sequence is constructed here, both being supplied by the hypothesis. So this
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-sequential-criterion-for-nonexistence.prompt.md-141-corollary, the workhorse for showing that a limit fails to exist, costs no
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-sequential-criterion-for-nonexistence.prompt.md-142-choice principle at all.
