research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-retry5-cex-psi-of-one-over-x-has-no-limit-at-zero.prompt.md-1249-implication from condition 1 to condition 2 of
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-retry5-cex-psi-of-one-over-x-has-no-limit-at-zero.prompt.md:1250:[[thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits]], which is a theorem of ZF; no
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-retry5-cex-psi-of-one-over-x-has-no-limit-at-zero.prompt.md-1251-sequence is constructed here, both being supplied by the hypothesis. So this
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-retry5-cex-psi-of-one-over-x-has-no-limit-at-zero.prompt.md-1252-corollary, the workhorse for showing that a limit fails to exist, costs no
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-retry5-cex-psi-of-one-over-x-has-no-limit-at-zero.prompt.md-1253-choice principle at all.
